      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-30568",
      ":question/problem": "A factory produces and sells diapers. The cost, $C(x)$, and revenue, $R(x)$, functions, in hundreds of dollars, for this company are\n$C(x) = 2000 + x, R(x) = 301x - 3x^{2}$,\nwhere $x$ denotes the number of units sold per month. Calculate the number of units the business should sell per month to maximize its monthly profit.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
